WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.558
The authors make three main contributions.

00:00:03.638 --> 00:00:07.197
First, they show that simple data augmentation,
random crop and flip,

00:00:07.277 --> 00:00:10.835
rebalances long-tailed multi-task data and improves
an autoregressive vision model just

00:00:10.915 --> 00:00:14.473
as effectively as collecting more real samples.

00:00:14.553 --> 00:00:18.112
Second,

00:00:18.192 --> 00:00:21.750
they bring knowledge distillation to autoregressive
large vision models for the first time,

00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:25.388
using a LLaMA one-billion teacher to lift a compact
three-hundred-million student across

00:00:25.468 --> 00:00:29.027
single-task and multi-task benchmarks.

00:00:29.107 --> 00:00:32.665
Third, they build a practical
eighty-million-parameter model that,

00:00:32.745 --> 00:00:36.303
combining both techniques,

00:00:36.383 --> 00:00:39.942
surprisingly reaches eighty-three percent top-one
accuracy on ImageNet,

00:00:40.022 --> 00:00:43.580
suggesting generation and understanding can be
learned together.
